# Model pair

`AGENTS.md` wins. Spawn a second model only when the user asks.

## Roles

- **Implementer** (Grok 4.6 groups by default): patch SoT and real package files. Own the write if both would touch the same path.
- **Mapper** (GPT 5.6 Luna 1M Max by default): wide consumer/duplicate/prelude scan. Return `CONFLICTS` / `SAFE_FIRST_FIXES` / `DO_NOT_TOUCH`. Do not rewrite SoT.

Same roles apply to GLM / Claude / others when the user names them.

## Thread (do not lose the work)

Canonical live pointer: `.progress/CURRENT.json`. Named-pass ledger: `.progress/<project>/STATE.json`.

1. Start: read `CURRENT.json`. Tag lookup: `MAP.json`. If `project` is a pass, also read that `STATE.json`.
2. Do not re-audit paths listed in `lastDone` / `paths` / MAP tags unless the user changed the goal or those files are gone.
3. Mapper: put `CONFLICTS` / `SAFE_FIRST_FIXES` / `DO_NOT_TOUCH` into `CURRENT.json` and new hubs into `MAP.json`. No parallel notes under aliases.
4. Implementer: apply one SoT or named-consumer patch. Then set `lastDone`, `next`, `paths`, `models.last`.
5. End of a meaningful turn: refresh `updatedAt`, `intent`, `status`. Keep `lastDone` to the last 3–5 facts.

Durable decisions that must survive weeks go to `.memories/`, not `CURRENT.json`.

## Shared

- Tokens: `.cursor/rules/design-tokens.mdc`. Library: `.cursor/rules/library-contracts.mdc`.
- Edit real files only. Alias leftover names. One implementation.
- Preserve wallpaper / `data-theme` / markdown contrast unless that theme is the task.

## Handoff

Mapper reports in `CURRENT.json`. Implementer applies. Mapper re-checks only that surface.
